SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: Training for New 
 MaineCare Partner Portal
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: Training for New MaineCare 
 Partner Portal\nAttention Trading Partners: Training for New MaineCare Par
 tner Portal\nSep 08\, 2026\nWe have\npreviously shared\nthat a refreshed a
 nd upgraded MIHMS\, with a new “MaineCare Partner Portal\,” is coming 
 in October 2026. This will replace the current HealthPAS Online Portal. 
 We are now inviting trading partners to\nregister for training that begin
 s September 8\, 2026\nto help you prepare for the transition to the new 
 portal. Trading partners include providers\, billing agents\, health plan
 s\, clearinghouses\, and business associates. Trading partners have an im
 portant role to play in supporting a smooth transition and uninterrupted 
 access to the portal after go-live.\nGainwell Technologies will be leadin
 g live virtual instructor-led training sessions. These courses will provid
 e the knowledge and skills needed to navigate the new portal\, complete da
 ily business functions\, and use new portal features. Training demonstrati
 ons\, materials\, and supporting resources will help participants prepare 
 for a successful transition.\nSteps you need to take to attend training\nR
 eview the available training topics listed below and identify the sessio
 ns that align with your role and responsibilities.\nUse the LMS registrati
 on (instructions below) to create an account\, access the training catalog
 \, and enroll in applicable sessions.\nContact Gainwell (instructions belo
 w) if you need assistance.\nRecorded sessions and other training material
 s will be available in the LMS after training sessions for ongoing referen
 ce.\nMaineCare Partner Portal Training Sessions\nCourse Name\nDescription\
 nME - TPT - Migrated Trading Partner Log In and Account Maintenance Trai
 ning (ILC)\nLearn how to complete first-time login activities\, configure 
 multi-factor authentication (MFA)\, manage user accounts and permissions\,
  perform accou\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletin
 s/attention-trading-partners-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-09
 -08
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-training-new-mainecare-partner-portal-2026-09-08
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
